from pathlib import Path
Path('/app/answer.json').write_text('{"answer": "It does not. Unconditional `self.accessed = True` in `SecureCookieSession.__getitem__`, `get`, and `setdefault` (`src/flask/sessions.py` lines 84-94) does not control signed-cookie conversion.\\n\\n`SecureCookieSessionInterface.save_session` uses `accessed` only to add a `Vary: Cookie` header (lines 362-364). Cookie serialization is gated by `should_set_cookie` (lines 247-261), which returns `session.modified or (session.permanent and app.config[\\"SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST\\"])`. When that is true, `save_session` calls `self.get_signing_serializer(app).dumps(dict(session))` (line 387).\\n\\nFrequent read-only requests pay dumps/HMAC cost when the session is permanent and `SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST` is true (default in `src/flask/app.py`). They do not pay it because dictionary reads set `accessed`. `session.permanent` itself calls `get(\\"_permanent\\")` and therefore sets `accessed`, but that still does not decide whether `dumps` runs."}' + '\n')
